# Exceptions to the cleanup checks: <kind> <path glob> -- <reason> (README, Quality Checks).
# Every entry reads <type> <key> -- <reason> -- <expiry>, with exactly two ' -- ' separators. The expiry is the last field and is exactly one of: permanent (counted in the check output; the owner approves each kind of permanent entry), expires YYYY-MM-DD (valid through that UTC date) or expires-when path-absent:<glob> (expired once no tracked file matches; no spaces in the glob). The reason may not contain the words expires or permanent. The expiry field is the only expiry the check reads; the reason is free text and is not interpreted. A missing, malformed or expired expiry is a finding.
